  * Foundation, Inc., 51 Franklin St, Fifth Floor, Boston, MA 02110-1301, USA
+ *
+ * Android has no OSS device nodes, no ALSA userspace and no PulseAudio
+ * daemon; the one native audio API an NDK process can use is AAudio
+ * (libaaudio.so, API 26+). Rather than wire a brand-new driver directory
+ * through configure, this file keeps wineoss.drv's name and its entire
+ * mmdevapi unixlib scaffolding - the local ring buffer, the period timer
+ * thread, the wow64 thunks - and swaps the device layer underneath from
+ * /dev/dsp ioctls to an AAudioStream. mmdevapi already probes "oss" in its
+ * default driver list, so nothing else has to learn a new name.
+ *
+ * The accounting maps one-to-one: where OSS asked SNDCTL_DSP_GETOSPACE how
+ * much of its buffer is filled, AAudio answers with the difference between
+ * AAudioStream_getFramesWritten() and AAudioStream_getFramesRead(); where
+ * OSS write()s into /dev/dsp, AAudioStream_write() with a zero timeout is
+ * the same non-blocking contract. MIDI and the OSS mixer-based aux devices
+ * have no Android equivalent and are stubbed to "no devices".
  */
 
